    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d360">

                <pb facs="0556" n="446" sameAs="frus:frus1928v03/pg446"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/5296: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Munro</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-01-22T13:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 22,
                                1928—1 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>26. The following telegram has been received from Habana:</p>
                <p>[Here follows the text of telegram No. 13, January 21, 1928, 9 p.m., from the
                    Chairman of the American Delegation to the Sixth International Conference of
                    American States to the Secretary of State, printed <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >supra.</hi>]</p>
                <pb facs="0557" n="447" xml:id="pg447"/>
                <p>The Department would be pleased to receive your comment on these suggestions.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
